{{Term/Store|Upland Lindor||Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring location in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Upland Lindor'''|Map|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Upland Lindor'''|Map|TotK}}</ref>

==Features and Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Upland Lindor is located on the foothills of [[Lindor's Brow]] on [[Hyrule Ridge]]. The [[Footrace Check-In]], a camp inhabited by [[Konba]], has been set up on its western end. [[Maag No'rah Shrine]] is located on the eastern end of Upland Lindor, inside a cave that faces towards the [[Maritta Exchange Ruins]]. Alongside Lindor's Brow and [[Mount Rhoam]], Upland Lindor wraps around the northwestern side of [[Ludfo's Bog]].

During the "[[EX Champion Revali's Song]]" [[Main Quest]], which is exclusive to {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] Pack, [[Link]] is tasked with shooting an [[Arrow]] at [[Dinraal]]'s horn as it passes through [[Tanagar Canyon]].<ref>{{Cite|♪Wind's ally soars the land of cloud.<br/>{{Color BotW|Blue|Medoh}}'s Champion, swift and proud.♪<br/>♪The hero's power shall grow.<br/>Seek trials {{Color BotW|Blue|monuments}} show.♪<br/>♪One, {{Color BotW|Red|shoot the flame dragon's horn}}.<br/>Two, {{Color BotW|Red|race down a peak rings adorn}}.♪<br/>♪Three, {{Color BotW|Red|shoot four targets to win}}.<br/>Champion, the trials begin!♪|Kass|BotW}}</ref> When he does this, [[Shira Gomar Shrine]] will rise from the ground on the northern side of Upland Lindor.

A [[Stone Talus (Luminous)]] is embedded in the ground on the northeastern side of Upland Lindor.<ref>{{Cite|Upland Lindor<br/>{{Big|'''Stone Talus'''}}|N/A|BotW}}</ref> It will initially be dormant, but if [[Link]] approaches the Talus, it will stand up and begin to attack him. Additionally, while Dinraal does not fly over Upland Lindor directly, it gets close enough while in the Tanagar Canyon to create [[Wind]]s and [[Updraft]]s.

[[File:BotW Korok Seed Icon.png|left|40px]]
Three separate [[Korok Seed Puzzle]]s can be found on Upland Lindor. The first is a [[Jar]] in a [[Tree]]'s hollow north of the Footrace Check-In, which Link must destroy with either [[Archery]] or [[Remote Bomb]]s. The second Puzzle is a [[Natural Hiding Spot]], disguised as a [[Rock]] west of the Stone Talus (Luminous). The final is another Natural Hiding Spot, this time buried under a pile of rubble east of the Talus. If Link solves one of these Puzzles, a [[Korok]] will appear and give him a [[Korok Seed]].<ref>{{Cite|Yahaha! You found me!|Korok|BotW}}</ref>

